{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1034","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Little C Loves 3 II"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Little C loves number «"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"» very much. He loves all things about it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now he is playing a game on a chessboard of size $$$n \\times m$$$. The cell in the $$$x$$$-th row and in the $$$y$$$-th column is called $$$(x,y)$$$. Initially, The chessboard is empty. Each time, he places two chessmen on two different empty cells, the Manhattan distance between which is exactly $$$3$$$. The Manhattan distance between two cells $$$(x_i,y_i)$$$ and $$$(x_j,y_j)$$$ is defined as $$$|x_i-x_j|+|y_i-y_j|$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"He want to place as many chessmen as possible on the chessboard. Please help him find the maximum number of chessmen he can place."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A single line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n,m \\leq 10^9$$$) — the number of rows and the number of columns of the chessboard."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one integer — the maximum number of chessmen Little C can place."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, the Manhattan distance between any two cells is smaller than $$$3$$$, so the answer is $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, a possible solution is $$$(1,1)(3,2)$$$, $$$(1,2)(3,3)$$$, $$$(2,1)(1,3)$$$, $$$(3,1)(2,3)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1034B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1034/problem/B"}